From: s3fs-ebpf maintainers
Subject: [PATCH] asm: preserve caller-set Offset when Marshal has no extended-ALU marker

Upstream `Instruction.Marshal` unconditionally overwrites `ins.Offset`
with `newOffset` at the end of the ALU-op fixup block. `newOffset` is
only non-zero for `SDiv` / `SMod` / `MovSX{8,16,32}`, so every plain
`Mov` written back to the wire ends up with `Offset=0`.

This silently corrupts `bpf_addr_space_cast`. LLVM (with
`-mcpu=v3 -mattr=+addr_space_cast` on clang 19+) encodes it as

    opcode = BPF_MOV | BPF_ALU64 | BPF_X   (0xbf)
    off    = BPF_ADDR_SPACE_CAST = 1
    imm    = (from_as << 16) | to_as

which surfaces at cilium/ebpf's asm layer as a plain `Mov` instruction
carrying `Offset=1, Constant=1`. Marshal turns that into
`Mov r_dst = r_src, off=0, imm=1`, and the kernel verifier rejects it
with `BPF_MOV uses reserved fields` (kernel/bpf/verifier.c:14620 in
v6.12, inside the else-branch of the addr_space_cast dispatch).

Verified against Linux 6.12 with clang 20.1.2 and a bpf_arena-based
`__arena` pointer dereference. See s3fs-ebpf
docs/week2-implementation-notes.md §1 for the full write-up.

Repro (relative to cilium/ebpf's tree, once addr_space_cast tests exist
upstream — until then, cross-check against the s3fs-ebpf harness at
`make test-arena`):

  llvm-objdump-20 -d ... | grep addr_space_cast   # before load: OK
  # after Marshal:
  bpftool prog load ...                            # verifier: "BPF_MOV uses reserved fields"

Fix: only overwrite `ins.Offset` when the Marshaller itself has
computed a non-zero `newOffset` (i.e. one of the extended-ALU forms).
For every other ALU op the caller-set Offset must survive to the wire.

Signed-off-by: s3fs-ebpf maintainers

---

To apply against a cilium/ebpf checkout at v0.22.0 (or main, as of
2026-09-11 the same code exists), from the repo root:

    patch -p1 < cilium-ebpf-addr-space-cast-marshal.patch

Or, if you want a real commit for a fork/PR:

    git am cilium-ebpf-addr-space-cast-marshal.patch

---
 asm/instruction.go | 11 ++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/asm/instruction.go b/asm/instruction.go
--- a/asm/instruction.go
+++ b/asm/instruction.go
@@ -192,7 +192,16 @@ func (ins Instruction) Marshal(w io.Writer, bo binary.ByteOrder) (uint64, error)
 		if newOffset != 0 && ins.Offset != 0 {
 			return 0, fmt.Errorf("extended ALU opcodes should have an .Offset of 0: %s", ins)
 		}
-		ins.Offset = newOffset
+		// s3fs-ebpf patch: only overwrite ins.Offset when Marshal actually
+		// needs to encode an extended-ALU marker. Upstream unconditionally
+		// wipes Offset to 0 for plain Mov, which silently corrupts BPF's
+		// `bpf_addr_space_cast` (opcode 0xbf|ALU64|X + Offset=1 + imm=1)
+		// into an invalid `MOV r_dst = r_src, off=0, imm=1` that the
+		// verifier rejects with "BPF_MOV uses reserved fields". Preserve
+		// caller-set Offset when we have no marker of our own to emit.
+		if newOffset != 0 {
+			ins.Offset = newOffset
+		}
 	} else if atomic := ins.OpCode.AtomicOp(); atomic != InvalidAtomic {
 		ins.OpCode = ins.OpCode &^ atomicMask
 		ins.Constant = int64(atomic >> 8)
